<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848), Kunth (1869) & Chindapol et al. (2013) Scleractinian coral calice septal insertion & advection-diffusion morphogenesis — MorphoEval overall 91.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) remediated evaluation of `2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py` (consensus score 91.6/100, up from 52.4/100 in Pass 1). Implements the Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848) hexameral septal insertion law N_hex(k) = 6 * 2^(k-1) across cycles k=1..6 with decreasing cycle radial reach alpha_k, Kunth's Law (1869) Paleozoic Rugosa serial 4-fossula insertion N_rugosa(m) = 6 + 4*m, Chindapol et al. (2013) Péclet advection-diffusion boundary-layer symmetry breaking across Pe in {0, 1, 4, 16, 36} (with Pe=0 pure-diffusion symmetry control A_1=0.0000 and r=0.9964 vs sqrt(Pe)), 7-species cross-taxa Scleractinian scaling (r=0.9988, log2 slope=1.0000), and automated polar ridge segmentation of n=40 radiating septa (9.00 deg spacing, major/minor reach ratio 1.4368) on the SHA-256-locked Caryophyllia quadragenaria calice specimen, backed by 4 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems. Overall 91.4/100 (faithfulness 91.1, reproducibility 92.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit HEAD; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 90, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/coral_calice_septa_insertion_comparison.png: rendered output of 2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py at HEAD, image/png, 1000915 B, 2415×1551 px, artifact_sha256 d46e2020411ac23d8a58f9a256c532c8780211a5bd3dcbe83eabb56f22a084cc (sha256 d46e2020411ac23d8a58f9a256c532c8780211a5bd3dcbe83eabb56f22a084cc), spec_fingerprint 838f1452734ffec4b95f30098de1ca90f5c6e961cce22175354f682fa6865b61. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 838f1452734ffec4b95f30098de1ca90f5c6e961cce22175354f682fa6865b61; artifact_sha256: d46e2020411ac23d8a58f9a256c532c8780211a5bd3dcbe83eabb56f22a084cc; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/coral_calice_septa_insertion_reference.json=9984d41d12285bd0..., datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/scleractinian_coral_septa_specimen.jpg=904035c936843361..., datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/scout_manifest.json=325761c7cb0d58db...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-coral-calice-septa-insertion-audit." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the boundary-layer Péclet flux model to oscillatory wave surge (Keulegan-Carpenter number) to compare unidirectional current polarization against bidirectional reef surge.",
        "remediation needed: Extend the 2D corallite calice simulator to a 3D accreting turbinate/trochoid corallum mesh resolving internal endothecal dissepiments and synapticulae alongside radial septa." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.14e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

